e>Independent ancient polyploidy events in sister families Brassicaceae and Cleomaceae</article-title><source>Plant Cell</source><year>2006</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>1152</fpage><lpage>1165</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16617098</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B26"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simillion</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The hidden duplication past of <italic>Arabidopsis thaliana</italic></article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci.</source><year>2002</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>13627</fpage><lpage>1632</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12374856</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B27"><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stege</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gene trees and species trees: the gene-duplication problem is fixed-parameter tractable. In</article-title><year>1999</year><publisher-loc>Vancouver, Canada</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Springer</publisher-name><comment><italic>Proceedings of the 6th International Workshop on Algorithms and Data Structures, LNCS 1663</italic></comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="B28"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sterck</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>EST data suggest that poplar is an ancient polyploidy</article-title><source>New Phytol.</source><year>2005</year><volume>167</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15948839</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B29"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vandepoele</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Evidence that rice and other cereals are ancient a